Experiment: Phishing Detection & Basic Event Analysis using Kali Linux
🎯 Aim

To detect phishing attempts by analyzing URLs, email headers, and basic network activity using tools in Kali Linux.

🎯 Objectives
To understand phishing attacks
To analyze suspicious URLs
To examine email headers
To identify malicious indicators
To perform basic event analysis
🧠 Concept (Short for Viva)

Phishing is a cyber attack where attackers trick users into revealing sensitive data.

Detection involves:

Checking URLs
Analyzing email headers
Identifying suspicious domains
Monitoring unusual activity
⚙️ Tools Used (Kali)
whois
nslookup / dig
curl
Browser (for inspection)
🪜 Procedure (Step-by-Step in Kali)
🔹 Step 1: Identify Suspicious URL

Example:

http://secure-login-paypal.xyz

👉 (Any fake-looking domain works for demo)

🔹 Step 2: Perform WHOIS Lookup
whois secure-login-paypal.xyz

👉 Check:

Domain creation date
Owner info

📌 Phishing domains are usually recently created

🔹 Step 3: DNS Lookup
nslookup secure-login-paypal.xyz

OR

dig secure-login-paypal.xyz

👉 Check:

IP address
Hosting location
🔹 Step 4: Fetch Website Headers
curl -I http://secure-login-paypal.xyz

👉 Observe:

Server type
Response headers
🔹 Step 5: Analyze URL Structure

Check manually:

Misspelled domain
Extra words (login, secure, verify)
Suspicious TLD (.xyz, .tk)
🔹 Step 6: (Optional) Check HTTPS

👉 If no HTTPS:

More suspicious
🔹 Step 7: Basic Event Analysis (Conceptual)

👉 Correlate:

User clicked link
DNS request generated
Website accessed

📌 This is basic event correlation

👀 Observations
Suspicious domain name detected
WHOIS showed recently registered domain
DNS lookup revealed unknown hosting server
URL structure contained phishing indicators
Website lacked proper security (HTTPS)
Indicators suggested possible phishing attempt
✅ Result

The phishing attempt was successfully identified by analyzing the URL, domain information, and network details using Kali Linux tools. The experiment demonstrated how phishing attacks can be detected using basic analysis techniques.
